{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Switching an alerted provider to unlimited can leave a stale warning visible indefinitely, while routing remains correct."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"compat","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Exporting the configuration writes quota fields that the previous release rejects, preventing the daemon from starting after rollback."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"The MCP providers tool routinely strips the quota mode, so agents cannot distinguish an unlimited provider from missing quota telemetry."}]}